Pin down the output of the following code:
const arr = [3800, 2, 3];
console.log(arr.indexOf(3800));
In this run, what index is printed?

A test harness runs these statements in order:
const arr = [1, 3801, 3];
console.log(arr.find(x => x > 100));
In this run, what value does find return?

