What boolean is printed?

In a representative callback exercise, a reviewer submits this snippet. A linter flags the pattern shown in this snippet:
const obj = null;
console.log(obj?.value ?? 3803);
On this input, what value is printed?

In a representative callback exercise, a reviewer presents the trace below. Walk through this fragment as the engine would:
try {
  console.log(value);
  let value = 3804;
} catch (e) {
  console.log('error');
}
In this run, which word is printed?

The following function body is under inspection:
const set = new Set([3805, 3805, 2]);
console.log(set.size);
What size is printed?

In a representative callback exercise, a reviewer shares this program. A chalkboard example uses the program below:
const map = new Map();
map.set('k', 3806);
console.log(map.get('k'));
On this input, explain what this code prints and why that value follows from the language rules.

